375371.statement:
A **rectair** is the rectair family used in CRIM, and $\mathcal G$ denotes its Sprague–Grundy value. Let $r$ and $k$ be integers with $0\leq k<r$. **Square-rectair conjecture.**

$$
\mathcal G(R_{r,r}^k)=
\begin{cases}
0& r\text{ is even or }k<r-1,\\
1& r\in\{3,5\},\ r\text{ is odd, and }k=r-1,\\
2&\text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
$$

The conjecture extends the known values for several rectair families, but the source provides no proof or resolution.

